---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy — Empire Eyes"
  description="How Empire Eyes handles data on this website, its link pages, its mailing list and its ads."
>
  <main class="privacy">
    <nav class="privacy-nav">
      <a href="/">&larr; EMPIRE EYES</a>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="privacy-title">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="privacy-label">Last updated 24 November 2026</p>

    <section>
      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Empire Eyes is the music project of Matthew Quaglia, based in Adelaide, South Australia.
        For anything about this policy or your data, email
        <a href="mailto:mgmt@empire-eyes.com">mgmt@empire-eyes.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        empire-eyes.com doesn't use analytics, advertising cookies or tracking scripts. Fonts are
        loaded from Google Fonts, which receives your IP address and browser details to deliver them.
        The website itself doesn't collect or store any personal information.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Listening links and ads</h2>
      <p>
        We advertise our music on Facebook, Instagram and Threads. The ads link to landing pages
        hosted by SubmitHub Links, which list where to listen. Those pages use the Meta pixel and
        Meta's Conversions API to tell Meta when someone visits, taps a listening button or opens
        a streaming app. This can include your IP address, browser and device details, and Meta's
        own cookie identifiers.
      </p>
      <p>
        We use this only to measure how our ads perform and to show our music to people likely to
        enjoy it, including people who have already engaged with Empire Eyes. Meta handles this
        information under its own
        <a href="https://www.facebook.com/privacy/policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>.
        You can control the ads you see in your Facebook or Instagram ad preferences.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Mailing list</h2>
      <p>
        Our mailing list runs on Substack, which stores your email address under its own
        <a href="https://substack.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>.
        We may upload subscribers' email addresses to Meta to show our music to subscribers on
        Facebook and Instagram. Meta encrypts (hashes) the addresses before matching them and
        deletes them after matching. You can unsubscribe at any time from any email.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What we don't do</h2>
      <p>
        We don't sell or rent personal information, and we don't share it with anyone other than
        the services named above.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="data-deletion">
      <h2>Your data and deletion requests</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask what information we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete
        it, by emailing <a href="mailto:mgmt@empire-eyes.com">mgmt@empire-eyes.com</a>. We'll reply
        within 30 days. Our Meta business app doesn't store personal data of its own; any
        information Meta holds about you can also be managed or deleted in your Facebook or
        Instagram settings.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .privacy {
    max-width: var(--max-w);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem var(--gutter) 4rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .privacy-nav a,
  .privacy-label,
  .privacy h2 {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--dim);
  }
  .privacy-nav a {
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .privacy-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: normal;
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .privacy-label {
    margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
  }
  .privacy section {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 1.5rem 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .privacy h2 {
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }
  .privacy p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .privacy p a {
    color: var(--fg);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
</style>
